/name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ICHIKI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDO TETSUJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIKI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, TETSUJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>On the basis of the results of comparison between the threshold value of a uniform random number fed from a uniform random number generator and the pixel value of an original image signal, each pixel value of the original image signal is encoded. The encoded image signal thus generated is transferred. A decoding device having received the transferred data accumulates the encoded values in the transfer data for each kind corresponding to the pixel value in the original image signal and counts the number of accumulations to decode the encoded value corresponding to each pixel of the accumulated original image signals on the basis of the counted number.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>En fonction des résultats de la comparaison entre le seuil d'un nombre aléatoire uniforme fourni par un générateur de nombres aléatoires uniformes, et la valeur de pixel d'un signal d'image original, chaque valeur de pixel d'un signal d'image original est codée. Le signal d'image codé ainsi généré est transféré. Un dispositif de décodage ayant reçu les données transférées cumule les valeurs codées dans les données de transfert pour chaque type correspondant à la valeur de pixel dans le signal d'image original et compte le nombre d'accumulations pour décoder la valeur codée correspondant à chaque pixel des signaux d'image originaux en fonction du nombre compté.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>